RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ddeevvssttaatt__ggeettnnuummddeevvss(), ddeevvssttaatt__ggeettggeenneerraattiioonn(), and
     ddeevvssttaatt__ggeettvveerrssiioonn() function return the indicated sysctl variable, or -1
     if there is an error fetching the variable.

     The ddeevvssttaatt__cchheecckkvveerrssiioonn() function returns 0 if the kernel and userland
     ddeevvssttaatt versions match.  If they do not match, it returns -1.

     The ddeevvssttaatt__ggeettddeevvss() and ddeevvssttaatt__sseelleeccttddeevvss() functions return -1 in
     case of an error, 0 if there is no error, and 1 if the device list or se‐
     lected devices have changed.  A return value of 1 from ddeevvssttaatt__ggeettddeevvss()
     is usually a hint to re-run ddeevvssttaatt__sseelleeccttddeevvss() because the device list
     has changed.

     The ddeevvssttaatt__bbuuiillddmmaattcchh() function returns -1 for error, and 0 if there is
     no error.

     The ddeevvssttaatt__ccoommppuuttee__eettiimmee() function returns the computed elapsed time.

     The ddeevvssttaatt__ccoommppuuttee__ssttaattiissttiiccss() function returns -1 for error, and 0 for
     success.

     If an error is returned from one of the ddeevvssttaatt library functions, the
     reason for the error is generally printed in the global string
     _d_e_v_s_t_a_t___e_r_r_b_u_f which is DEVSTAT_ERRBUF_SIZE characters long.

